# Fedora's kernel headers standing in for linux-headers, a toolchain
# package, in a pos build without a toolchain reference: the bootstrap
# glibc of the first pos reference (BUILD.md "Toolchain"). linux-headers
# obsoletes it, so where a toolchain reference has linux-headers, its are
# used. gcc-host, which builds that glibc, searches /usr/include after
# /pos/include.
kind host
provides linux-headers
host-requires kernel-headers
